# git has no per-file revision number, so an RCS style ident line cannot be
# expanded the way cvs(1) expanded $NetBSD$.  export-subst is the one
# mechanism that needs no per-clone setup: git archive substitutes the
# $Format:...$ placeholders when it builds a tarball, which is exactly what a
# Homebrew formula fetches and unpacks.  A plain checkout shows the placeholder
# unexpanded; tests/check_ident.sh keeps the substitution honest.
stns.conf.example export-subst
ldapstns.conf.example export-subst
